From e64147e241f5744b38094e305efa4596da89d4e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Haseeb Ashraf <haseeb.ashraf@siemens.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 10:10:00 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] tools: Default to the GL renderer

With GTK 4.22 the default GSK renderer is Vulkan. On the Xen dom0
target (virtio-gpu guests, Weston) mks dumps core with it and only works
with GSK_RENDERER=gl in the environment.

Set GSK_RENDERER=gl before GTK is initialised, without overriding a
value the user exported, so that no environment setup is needed.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [workaround for a renderer problem on the target stack]
Signed-off-by: Haseeb Ashraf <haseeb.ashraf@siemens.com>
---
 tools/mks.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tools/mks.c b/tools/mks.c
index b12ec73..56766c8 100644
--- a/tools/mks.c
+++ b/tools/mks.c
@@ -277,6 +277,12 @@ main (int   argc,
   if (argc > 1)
     address = argv[1];
 
+  /* GTK 4.22 picks its Vulkan renderer by default, which crashes while it
+   * imports the guest's dmabuf scanouts (virtio-gpu / Venus hosts). Use the
+   * GL renderer unless the user explicitly chose one with GSK_RENDERER.
+   */
+  g_setenv ("GSK_RENDERER", "gl", FALSE);
+
   gtk_init ();
   mks_init ();
 
